.TH OROC-BUILD 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.2.0" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-build \- Build Oro application.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc build [options] [<project\-or\-source>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Build Oro application.
.PP
Provide a project directory, HTML file, or JavaScript module. When no oro.toml is found, oroc infers a minimal configuration automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-platform=<platform>\fR
platform target to build application for (defaults to host):
.br
\(bu android
.br
\(bu android\-emulator
.br
\(bu ios
.br
\(bu ios\-simulator
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
use an explicit oro.toml/oro.ini file
.TP
\fB\-\-device=<serial>\fR
Android device to install and run on
.TP
\fB\-\-copy=<source:dest>\fR
extra copy mapping (like [build] copy; can be repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-port=<port>\fR
load "index.html" from a specific port (if host is not specified, defaults to localhost)
.TP
\fB\-\-host=<host>\fR
load "index.html" from a specific host (if port is not specified, defaults to 80)
.TP
\fB\-t, \-\-test=<path>\fR
enable test mode and import a test file relative to resource files
.TP
\fB\-H, \-\-headless\fR
build application to run in headless mode (without frame or window)
.TP
\fB\-P, \-\-prod\fR
build for production (disables debugging info, inspector, etc.)
.TP
\fB\-D, \-\-debug\fR
enable debug mode
.TP
\fB\-E, \-\-env=<name[=value]>\fR
add environment variables
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-only\-build\fR
only run the build step
.TP
\fB\-p, \-\-package\fR
package the app for distribution
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
hint for less log output
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-run\fR
run after building
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-verbose\fR
enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-w, \-\-watch\fR
watch for changes to rerun build step
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-exec\fR
allow native extension commands (git/build scripts)
.TP
\fB\-\-sanitizers\fR
enable developer sanitizers (ASan/UBSan) for desktop core builds
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\fR
enable all supported build result caches (default: off)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
disable supported build result caches for this build
.TP
\fB\-\-compiler\-cache\fR
enable ccache/sccache for native object compilation
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-compiler\-cache\fR
disable the native compiler cache
.TP
\fB\-\-android\-cache\fR
enable all supported caches for Android builds
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-android\-cache\fR
disable supported caches for Android builds
.TP
\fB\-\-android\-build\-cache\fR
enable Gradle's task output cache
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-android\-build\-cache\fR
disable Gradle's task output cache
.TP
\fB\-\-android\-configuration\-cache\fR
enable Gradle's configuration cache
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-android\-configuration\-cache\fR
disable Gradle's configuration cache
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-keylog=<path>\fR
write NSS TLS key log lines to <path> (OpenSSL provider)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.TP
\fB\-\-editor\-project=<dir>\fR
export an Android editor project
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\-debugging\-port=<port>\fR
set the remote debugging port
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
show help
.SH LINUX OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-package\-format=<format>\fR
package a Linux application in a specified format for distribution:
.br
\(bu deb (default)
.br
\(bu rpm
.br
\(bu zip
.br
\(bu aur (generate AUR PKGBUILD only)
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\fR
sign Linux packages with GPG (writes .asc next to the artifact)
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-key=<id>\fR
optional GPG key ID or fingerprint to use with '\-\-sign' (letters/digits/@._\- only)
.SH MACOS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-codesign\fR
code sign application with 'codesign'
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-notarize\fR
notarize application with 'notarytool'
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-package\-format=<format>\fR
package a macOS application in a specified format for distribution:
.br
\(bu zip (default)
.br
\(bu pkg
.SH IOS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-codesign\fR
code sign application during xcodebuild (requires '[ios] provisioning_profile' in your config file)
.SH WINDOWS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-package\-format=<format>\fR
package a Windows application in a specified format for distribution:
.br
\(bu appx (default)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBORO_ALLOW_EXEC\fR
allow native extension commands during builds
.TP
\fBORO_ENABLE_SANITIZERS\fR
enable ASan/UBSan on desktop builds
.SH NOTES
.PP
Relative paths are resolved from the project root or from the directory containing the explicit `\-\-config` file when one is supplied. `\-\-prod` controls packaging/debug defaults; `\-\-package` controls whether a distributable artifact is produced in addition to the build output directory.
.PP
Use `\-\-copy` for one\-off extra bundle mappings without modifying `oro.toml`.
.PP
Cache flags override oro.toml; specific cache flags override broader cache flags.
.PP
Set [build] cache=true for a project default, [android] cache=true for Android only, or [android] configuration_cache=true for only Gradle configuration caching.
.PP
Use compiler_cache in [build] or a platform section to control native object caching.
.PP
Compiler caching uses ccache/sccache from PATH and compiles directly if neither is installed.
.PP
Download caches and existing incremental build behavior retain their toolchain defaults.
.PP
Android run targets use \-\-device, then ANDROID_SERIAL, then the first ready device listed by `adb devices`. The android\-emulator target selects the first ready emulator.
.PP
NO_ANDROID and NO_IOS do not control this application build command. They are independent, presence\-based exclusions for runtime source bootstrap (`bin/install.sh` / `npm run relink`).
.SH COMMON ERRORS
.PP
Android builds: run `oroc setup \-\-platform=android` and accept SDK licenses. macOS/iOS signing: set `[ios] provisioning_profile`/specifier or `[mac.productbuild] identity` in your config file.
.PP
Standard Android builds run NDK and Gradle automatically. Native extension commands may require `\-\-allow\-exec` or `ORO_ALLOW_EXEC=1`.
.SH LINUX DEPENDENCIES
.PP
deb packaging requires `dpkg` and `fakeroot` (e.g., `sudo apt\-get install dpkg\-dev fakeroot`). rpm packaging requires `rpmbuild` (e.g., `sudo dnf install rpm\-build`).
.SH MACOS DEPENDENCIES
.PP
Xcode and Command Line Tools are required (`xcode\-select \-\-install`). For Gradle/JDK: `brew install gradle openjdk` (or use SDKMAN).
.SH WINDOWS DEPENDENCIES
.PP
Windows 10/11 SDK and Visual Studio Build Tools are recommended. Ensure `signtool.exe` is available (set SIGNTOOL or add SDK bin to PATH).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc build .\fR
build the current project for the host platform
.TP
\fBoroc build \-r \-\-debug .\fR
rebuild and immediately run a debug build
.TP
\fBoroc build \-\-platform=ios \-\-prod \-\-package .\fR
produce a signed/package\-ready iOS build using your config
.TP
\fBoroc build \-\-copy assets:assets .\fR
include an extra assets directory in the bundle for this build only
.TP
\fBoroc build \-\-platform=android \-\-cache \-\-no\-android\-configuration\-cache .\fR
enable supported caches except Gradle configuration caching
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
